==English==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|LL.|realia}}, neuter plural of {{m|la|realis||real}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ɹeɪˈɑːlɪə/|/ɹiːˈeɪlɪə/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑːliə|eɪliə|s=4}}

===Noun===
{{en-plural noun}}

# Objects from real life or from the real world, as opposed to [[theoretical]] [[constructs]] or [[fabricated]] examples.
#* '''2011''', {{w|Norman Davies}}, ''Vanished Kingdoms'', Penguin 2012, p. 28:
#*: It might be possible, for example, to work backwards from the known '''realia''' of Visigothic Spain.

